<title>ITALY: Parmalat reopens down after Ault deal.</title>
<headline>Parmalat reopens down after Ault deal.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Italy's largest listed food company Parmalat resumed trade after temporary suspension on the Milan bourse down around five percent after it had announced an accord to take over Canadian food group Ault Foods.</p>
<p>Earlier, Ault Foods Ltd said it had agreed to a take over by Parmalat for C$34 per share, or C$415 million in total.</p>
<p>Parmalat shares had been suspended pending the announcement and was last quoted off 6.43 percent at 2,300 lire at 1447 GMT.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
